      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "Subject: Request for Complete Secure Software Development Framework Specification Aligned to NIST SP 800-218 v1.1\n\nTeam, we need a comprehensive secure software development specification document for our organization that fully maps to the four practice groups defined in the NIST Secure Software Development Framework version 1.1\u2014Prepare the Organization, Protect the Software, Produce Well-Secured Software, and Respond to Vulnerabilities. The specification should cover people, processes, and technology requirements at the organizational level for each practice group, define specific implementation tasks for each SSDF practice and sub-practice, and establish roles and responsibilities for our development, security, and operations teams. Please incorporate references to supplementary guidance such as SAFECode's resources on practical SDL adoption and Microsoft's simplified SDL implementation approach to provide our teams with actionable onboarding material. The spec must address how we tailor each practice to our current toolchain (GitHub Enterprise, Jenkins CI/CD, SonarQube, and Jira) and outline a phased rollout plan starting with highest-risk product lines. Include acceptance criteria for each practice group so that our internal audit team can verify conformance during quarterly reviews. We need a first complete draft ready for leadership review by end of next quarter, with stakeholder feedback incorporated into a final version within three weeks after that review cycle closes.",
